arting up and you're a  one-person show  but you know your highest value is going  to come from doing the things that  you're really good at and you love  and you want to start delegating off the  low value stuff  that still needs to get done in your  business but it shouldn't be you doing  it  so part-time workers interns  i brought on you know high school and  college interns and foreign language  interns  i've brought on again part-time workers  i've used  websites like odesk and elance odessa is  my favorite now though they've merged so  i don't know what that relationship  looks like but  i still have a team on odesk that i love  and do great work including christina  who does all these videos thank you  christine i love you  i've even had people who are who are  fans so  i've done uh you know people who are who  are active in my community and who like  what i stand for they want to find ways  to help  just to volunteer there's this arturo  who takes some of these videos and  translates them into spanish  just because he feels like spanish  entrepreneurs need to  get this entrepreneurial education and  there's kevin  uh who you know wants to learn how to be  an entrepreneur wants to help out on  some of the projects i'm working on so  he's he's hopping on some stuff  so when you stand for something  important when people believe in what  you're doing  when something powerful something that  means something to them don't want to  get involved and help out  and the last thought that i have for you  is  look at creating joint ventures and so  you know you're bringing somebody on to  your team  you have to decide is somebody who's  going to be just an employee or somebody  who i'm comfortable doing a partnership  with  and a lot of the stuff i've done in my  business is i've partnered with people  on specific projects so i own my  business hundred percent i don't have  investors i don't have partners it's  just me  but i have jv's joined venture ships  with  a number of people on specific projects  and so  that all works differently could be 50  50 70 30. whatever  you know ratio you think makes the most  sense is simply going to be based on how  much  each person brings to the table but  you're not spending a lot of money  to do this or any money to do this  they're investing their time but you  have to make sure people get paid  for what they're doing right so if  they're going to invest a lot of their  time up front  and not get any payment they got to get  something to return on the end which is  some kind of joint ventureship in the  project i'd be hesitant to give up  a percentage of your business unless you  feel the person is really really really  really really the right fit for your  company  that's my advice thanks for all the  comments believe because you're watching  like the video please give it a thumbs  up below  let me know what you think ask a  question  tell me how to feel better leave in the  comments below and you can click on my  face to subscribe to the channel  thank you so much i'll see you soon
 

